1
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:11,700
I dropped a painting.

2
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:36,200
I came in early that morning.

3
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:38,850
It was hanging crooked, only a little.

4
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,160
So I straightened it.

5
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:45,300
And, well. You can see.

6
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:47,000
It came off the wall.

7
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:48,540
There's a hole there now.

8
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:51,500
I called the plasterer straight away
to patch it.

9
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:52,940
Is this the contractor?

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,140
Yes. How can we help?

11
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:55,600
Can you come now?

12
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,500
What's the emergency?

13
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:58,900
Please.

14
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:06,300
Good morning. The Valder Collection
opens to visitors in five minutes.

15
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:10,000
Then the first customer
walked into this room.

16
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:21,000
Excuse me, sir.

17
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:25,300
What happened to the wall?

18
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:27,200
Sorry, sir.

19
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:33,800
That is art. I like it.

20
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:38,370
What are you looking at?
There is nothing there.

21
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:40,800
I am looking at art.

22
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,950
It is clearly about labour.

23
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:44,780
It is a crack.

24
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:47,020
Exactly what they want you to think.

25
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:48,800
It made me think of my mother.

26
00:01:48,850 --> 00:01:49,820
Do not touch it!

27
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,400
I am measuring it.

28
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,700
We are going to be late.

29
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:57,100
[everyone talking at once]

30
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,510
Good morning.

31
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:02,600
Welcome, all of you,
to the Valder Collection.

32
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:05,500
Mr Valder should be with us very shortly.

33
00:02:05,650 --> 00:02:07,350
I would like to buy this piece.

34
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:09,200
Two million.

35
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,600
Of course, madam. Of course.

36
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,400
I will fetch Mr Valder at once.

37
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:32,300
Five million.

38
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:35,100
I will give you five million for it.

39
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:41,100
Forgive me, sir.
May I take your name?

40
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:43,500
Carrington.

41
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,600
Mr Carrington, of course.

42
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:50,700
You did not tell us you were coming.

43
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:52,950
I would have received you properly.

44
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:55,400
I will contact Mr Valder at once.

45
00:03:07,830 --> 00:03:10,050
Good morning. Good morning, everyone.

46
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:11,900
It is a very good day.

47
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:14,200
Ah, Mr Carrington, there you are.

48
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:16,150
You did not tell me you were coming?

49
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:17,790
I'd have received you properly.

50
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,570
This room was just rearranged.

51
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:21,650
Come, let me show you everything.

52
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:25,390
Everything in this wing
was rehung only last week.

53
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:28,090
I think you will like
what I have done.

54
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:30,610
All acquired in the last two years.

55
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:33,200
But I kept the best of it for you.

56
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:37,220
This chair was there when the
armistice was signed.

57
00:03:37,270 --> 00:03:41,520
Not at the table. In the corner.
Nobody sat in it.

58
00:03:41,570 --> 00:03:45,000
A fish trap.
It caught nothing for forty years.

59
00:03:45,050 --> 00:03:48,040
The man who made it
never sold a single one.

60
00:03:48,190 --> 00:03:51,600
Excuse me. Are you following us with that?

61
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,500
And this one.

62
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:08,000
I did not commission it.
I did not buy it.

63
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:13,000
It happened to my wall
while nobody was looking.

64
00:04:13,050 --> 00:04:16,600
That one decided by itself.

65
00:04:16,690 --> 00:04:23,100
I have been collecting for forty years
to find something that did not need me.

66
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:25,700
Mr Valder. I want it.

67
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:29,300
Of course you do. Everybody does.

68
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:44,200
There she is. At last.

69
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,300
Ten million.

70
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:51,300
Fifteen.

71
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:54,300
Twenty million.

72
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:57,200
Twenty-five.

73
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,600
Fifty.

74
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:13,200
One hundred million.

75
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:27,800
One hundred million dollars
for a crack in a wall.

76
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:32,300
The collector, Maximilian Valder,
declined to comment.

77
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:46,800
Do you know what you were about to do?

78
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:48,400
Fill a crack, sir.

79
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,600
Yes.

80
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:51,600
How much were you offered?

81
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:53,050
Eight hundred.

82
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:55,300
I will give you eight thousand.

83
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:56,640
To fix it?

84
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:58,700
To have never come.

85
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:04,800
Someone asked me to fix it.

86
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:17,300
STOP! You are destroying
a hundred million dollar artwork!

87
00:06:18,490 --> 00:06:20,700
I thought they were going to fire me.

88
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:37,600
So I had to do something.

89
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,140
Sorry, sir.

90
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:43,300
I cracked it. Last hour.

91
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:47,400
I cracked the wall myself, sir.

92
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,600
I will pay for all the damage.

93
00:06:49,750 --> 00:06:50,830
I am sorry.

94
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:53,600
Then the artist is the building.

95
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:57,600
I did not buy a crack in a wall.

96
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:00,400
I bought a work of art.

97
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:06,900
One hundred million.

98
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:13,700
But that is my wall!

99
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:14,900
I should have it!

100
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,600
I did not pay for the wall.

101
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,600
I paid the artist who made it.

102
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,900
Good morning.
The museum is now open.

103
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:59,600
That is art. I like it.
